---
id: org.dxos.review.echo
name: Echo
version: 0.1.0
---

ECHO object-graph conventions a linter cannot express. Each `rule` block below
is discovered by the agentic-review harness.

## Extensions

| Term   | URI                   |
| ------ | --------------------- |
| `rule` | org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0 |

## Rules

```mdl
rule inline-obj-parent: Set parent at make time with [Obj.Parent]
  When the parent is already known at construction, pass it inline as
  `[Obj.Parent]: parent` on `Obj.make` (or a type factory that forwards to it)
  rather than `Obj.make(...)` followed by `Obj.setParent(obj, parent)`. Inline
  parent is the supported make-time API and keeps the cascade edge on the same
  statement as the object. Flag a newly created object that is then immediately
  parented with `Obj.setParent` when that parent was in scope at `make`. Do not
  flag `Obj.setParent` used to reparent or unparent an *existing* object, to
  set parent to `undefined`, or when the parent is only determined after
  construction (conditional, async lookup). Do not flag comments or docs that
  mention `Obj.setParent`.
  scope: repo
  files:
    - packages/**/*.ts
    - packages/**/*.tsx
  grep: Obj\.setParent
  severity: warn
```

```mdl
rule obj-update-push: Append inside Obj.update with push, not spread
  Inside `Obj.update`, append to an object array with `.push` (or `.unshift` /
  `.splice` for insert-at-index). Do not assign a spread copy
  (`arr = [...arr, item]`, `arr = [...arr, ...items]`, `arr = arr.concat(...)`)
  — Automerge array spread is O(n) per append; `push` is O(1). Canonical
  example: `Obj.update(set, (set) => { set.tasks.push(Ref.make(task)); })`.
  Flag a spread/concat assign of an object's own array field inside an
  `Obj.update` callback (or an equivalent in-place mutation block on a live
  proxy). Do not flag replacing the array with a *different* sequence
  (`filter`, `map`, reorder, slice-out) — that is not an append. Do not flag
  spreads of local non-proxy arrays, or spreads outside `Obj.update`.
  scope: repo
  files:
    - packages/**/*.ts
    - packages/**/*.tsx
  grep: Obj\.update
  severity: warn
```

## Appendix

```mdl
ext rule
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.rule@1.0
  desc: A machine-checked review rule applied by an LLM subagent to changed files.
  inline-prose: true
  fields:
    files:      Glob | Glob[]     # paths this rule reviews, relative to `scope`
    grep?:      Prose             # optional regex pre-filter over file contents
    severity?:  warn | error      # defaults to warn
    scope?:     dir | repo        # glob base: this file's dir (default) or repo root
```
